      "id": 199662,
      "name": "Chaosmancer",
      "username": "Chaosmancer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-07-27T20:34:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And last but not least Unity has left behind the 'grease monkey' look for something more like a super suit, still rocking with the pink.&nbsp;Over all I like the new looks. I'm excited to start reading and see what other visual changes may have happened to other heroes! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Got to say, I like this outfit more than the Tactics one for unity, probably because the metal ribbing makes it look more like a suit of armor, but her original look is still the best. Possibly Termi-NAtion is better, but everytime I see her in a pink latex jumpsuit instead of clothing I just twinge a little inside. I like her as the type of person who heroes in their everyday street clothes, it just feels like that's what she would do</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:27:47.883Z",
